WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.701
-Quickly, today's a little
anniversary for us.

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:07.067
It's been -- 13 years ago,
we started late night.

00:00:07.067 --> 00:00:09.334
-13?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.334 --> 00:00:12.400
Wow.
That's a long --

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:13.634
13?

00:00:13.634 --> 00:00:15.868
-13 years ago, yeah.
March 2nd, so yeah.

00:00:15.868 --> 00:00:18.334
-Now it's a teenager.
-Yeah. Exactly, yeah.

00:00:18.334 --> 00:00:20.501
So, 13 years ago,
we actually made --

00:00:20.501 --> 00:00:23.000
we made a yearbook.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.601
Because we were so excited just
to be on the air for a year.

00:00:26.601 --> 00:00:28.801
We didn't think we'd
go further than a year.

00:00:28.801 --> 00:00:31.234
So, we were so excited.

00:00:31.234 --> 00:00:34.734
We made a fake yearbook.
"Learning to Fly" is our theme.

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:37.400
What I love -- I was looking
at it today, just going --

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:41.467
2009, the first year,
we dedicated to --

00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:45.067
to Wayne Federman, who's
a great comedian, and then --

00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:46.767
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah, and then

00:00:46.767 --> 00:00:49.968
if you go down here, it's
a rebuttal to the dedication,

00:00:49.968 --> 00:00:52.067
'cause he's still alive,
and so we just --

00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:54.901
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.901 --> 00:00:57.234
And here's --
This is one thing I kept.

00:00:57.234 --> 00:01:01.033
I hang it on my office wall
just to keep me grounded,

00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:02.801
'cause you can't get a big head
in this business,

00:01:02.801 --> 00:01:03.968
no matter what.

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:05.467
You get so excited.
You go, "Oh, my gosh.

00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:07.834
I got late night,
and this is such a big deal."

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:11.868
And, you know,
I got to thank Conan O'Brien

00:01:11.868 --> 00:01:13.534
for keeping the show on the air.

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:16.501
He did 16 years.
David Letterman.

00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:17.868
-Yep.
-Unbelievable.

00:01:17.868 --> 00:01:19.834
I wouldn't have a job
if it wasn't for those guys.

00:01:19.834 --> 00:01:21.467
And I was just so excited
I got my thing,

00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:22.667
and then I get to my office,

00:01:22.667 --> 00:01:24.934
and this is hanging
in front of my office.

00:01:24.934 --> 00:01:26.334
Can you see this?
No glare?

00:01:26.334 --> 00:01:28.334
They spelled my name wrong.
-Yeah.

00:01:28.334 --> 00:01:29.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.667 --> 00:01:31.300
-"Jimmy Falon."
-Yeah.

00:01:32.901 --> 00:01:34.701
-Jimmy Falon.
-Jimmy Falon.

00:01:34.701 --> 00:01:36.067
"Who's the new guy?"

00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:39.300
-Yeah, NBC is like, "Yeah,
you'll get there one day, yeah."

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:40.901
I was like, "Don't take it off.
Don't change that.

00:01:40.901 --> 00:01:43.000
I gotta save that," so, anyways,

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.434
thanks to everyone
who worked on that show

00:01:45.434 --> 00:01:47.767
and everyone for watching us
for all these years.

00:01:47.767 --> 00:01:49.667
I appreciate it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:49.667 --> 00:01:51.234
Fun times.

00:01:51.234 --> 00:01:52.467
Here we are.

